/-!
# The Window Tower of Spec ℤ

Umbrella for the theory of the tower `A ↦ W_A` of windows of the scaling line: the window
representation of the Dirichlet ring and the window algebra (truncated Dirichlet ring); the tower of
small extensions (one new fold per stage, socle law, Loewy length, primes as cotangent space,
Dirichlet ring as inverse limit); Weil's window form as the derivative at dimension zero of the
Jordan counts (Tate pieces); the Tate flow, its cocycle and the commutator form of the Tate
operators, Tate positivity and its softness; the atomic lattice as the regular representation of
the window algebra; the exact pole capacity and the sharp window floor; the symmetries of the
tower (Adams lifts as dilations, Serre duality as the Rosati involution); completely multiplicative
twists (Tate flow, characters) and the character-weighted Tate pieces of `L(s, χ)`; Weil's window
form as a signed combination of projective point counts (interpolation of `log`); the transfer
across a stage and the collar exit charge paying every new fold. See
`WindowTowerOfSpecZ/README.md`.
-/
